  "oracleRepeatDiagnosticInterpretation": {
    "observations": "The baseline continuous realm is bit-exact over six renders. Fresh baseline realms differ by scene max1..2 and post max1 despite equal recorded command traces, Canvas initial state, actual measureText widths and loaded FontFace states. Adding only --disable-accelerated-2d-canvas makes all twelve oracle scene/post repeats bit-exact in this bounded trial.",
    "limits": "This is an instrumented oracle-only experiment, not acceptance. Observation can affect timing. Object arguments record identities/types/dimensions, not underlying CanvasPattern/image pixels. Equal command traces and FontFace status therefore do not prove identical hidden browser cache/raster state, all font raster state, or all texture pixels. The structural max40 drift was not reproduced here. The flag intervention supports a browser Canvas/backend contribution but does not establish a specific Chromium defect or the cause of every historical run."
  },
